{
  "_comment": "Per-faction unit and ship names, the stat trade a distinctive name carries, and the two small bonuses every realm has. Owner-specified in 0.20.0 and REWRITTEN in 0.20.1 to be readable rather than authentic: the owner's note was that most of the first pass was 'very specific to that nation' and that names should be 'understandable by everyone'.",
  "_rule": "A SHARED PLAIN NAME IS THE DEFAULT. Man-at-Arms, Spearman, Crossbowman, Knight, Halberdier, Horse Archer, Cog, Galley, Carrack, Galleon — most realms use these and most realms share them, which is what the owner asked for and what history supports. A DISTINCTIVE NAME IS THE EXCEPTION, kept only where the unit is one a general audience recognises: Longbowman, Janissary, Sipahi, Gendarme, Coustillier, Landsknecht, Hussar, Cossack, Mamluk, Cataphract, Varangian Guard, Genoese Crossbowman, Jinete, Mangudai, Caravel, Galleass.",
  "_trades": "Only a distinctive name carries a stat trade. A realm calling its swordsmen Man-at-Arms has not changed the unit, so it gets the base figures unchanged; a realm fielding Longbowmen has, and pays for it. Deltas are added to the base in data/units.json. Only hp, damage and strategicSpeed may vary — cost, size, upkeep and build time are identical in every realm.",

